        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "n9K7h",
          "x": 580,
          "y": 300,
          "name": "spec_notes",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 376,
          "content": "NEW CHAT ROW — cmp/SidebarNewChat, the first row of WORKSPACE, above runner and crew (Jason, 2026-08-23). Same 216 × 28 geometry and [6,10] padding as the nav rows: icon message-square-plus 12 in $accent, label Inter 14/600 in $text-mid, ⌘N hint 11/500 in $text-low at the right. No fill at rest; hover $sidebar-sel like the nav rows; it is an action, never a selected page. Click = the existing NewChat(None) action (Start Chat modal). The RECENT “+” stays as the secondary affordance. Considered and rejected: an accent-filled button under the brand (right — too loud) and the same row standing alone between the brand and WORKSPACE (reads as a third section).\n\nPROJECT ROW “+” — appears with the kebab on hover/focus of a project row, same 12 px glyph and $text-mid ink as the RECENT header “+”, 8 px before the 14 px ellipsis; $text-hi on the hovered row. Click opens the two-item menu shown over the row — “New chat” → NewChat(Some(project)), “New mission” → NewMission(Some(project)); the labels drop the kebab's “in project” qualifier because the menu hangs off the row itself. The kebab keeps its longer labels. Collapsed projects behave the same.\n\nROW MENUS — tab rows and mission rows lose “Open in New Window” and “Remove from project”; Pin / Rename tab / Archive remain, Archive in the danger ink. Both capabilities survive elsewhere: ⇧⌘N plus a sidebar pick opens a session in another window; dragging a row to RECENT moves it out of a project.\n\nTOKENS — sidebar $sidebar, rows 216 × 28 with [6,10] padding and radius 4, hovered row $sidebar-sel, section heads Inter 10/600 +1.5 tracking $text-low, menus $panel / $line-strong / radius 8 / 32 px items, hover item $raised.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
