          "content": "PILL — cmp/TabShortcutPill: 16 × 16, $raised fill, radius 4, digit JetBrains Mono 10/500 in $text-mid. It sits in the row's trailing slot (x 190 of the 216 row, the kebab's place) and REPLACES whatever lives there while ⌘ is held: the pin glyph, the unread dot, the mission status glyph, the hover kebab. Label width shrinks by the slot difference; long labels ellipsize as they do today.\n\nNUMBERING — 1…9 top to bottom over the rows a click could activate, in display order: PINNED rows, then each expanded project's children (chats and missions), then RECENT. Project header rows, the WORKSPACE nav, and children of a collapsed project (quill, pulse here) get no number and no pill. Ten or more rows: 1–9 only, the rest show nothing. No ⌘0.\n\nSTATES — selected row (Codex, $sidebar-sel fill): the pill stays neutral — $raised chip, digit in $text-hi so it reads on the lighter fill. Decided: NO accent inversion; accent is reserved for attention and busy. Unread row (@investing): dot gives way to the pill, label stays $text-hi. Busy mission (M6.15): status glyph gives way to the pill. Rows with nothing in the slot simply gain the pill.\n\nTIMING — pills appear after ⌘ has been held alone for ~150 ms (ordinary chords ⌘C / ⌘N / ⌘K never flash them) and vanish the instant ⌘ is released, another modifier joins, or the window loses focus. ⌘N jumps exactly as a click would (route to Chat + activate the tab; route to the mission for a mission row) — per window, global, rebindable as select-tab-1…9; with the sidebar collapsed the jump still works and nothing is shown.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "xIl71",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1645,
      "name": "chatFeatureSpecsLbl",
      "fill": "$text-mid",
      "content": "feature specs — ⌘1–9 (M6.15) · sidebar entry points (M6.21) · fork (60) · pane × archives (567) · split panes (570) · drag to reorder (568) · terminal split (574)",
      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "F0ComJ",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Fork chat (60) · side panel button",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 660,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "cornerRadius": 12,
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "p3O7M4",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Fork chat (feature 60, #398) · sidebar row icon + chat header icon",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SNiHA",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "content": "Two entry points, one destination: a ⑂ icon on the sidebar chat row (hover) and a ⑂ icon in the chat header; a fork always opens as a new tab (new node). claude-code + codex only (native fork); trae/shell never.",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T5pntD",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 440,
          "name": "cap_notes",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "BEHAVIOUR",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tt67D",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 460,
          "name": "notes",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1052,
          "content": "Both icons call the same fork_chat → runner-backend session_fork: a new session row cloned from the source chat (runner, runtime, cmd, cwd, model/effort), spawned natively — claude-code `--resume <key> --fork-session`, codex `fork <key>` — with no first turn. The source row, key, PTY and transcript are never written. The fork opens as a NEW TAB (a new node) titled \"<source label> (fork)\", active and focused; the source tab is untouched. The fork's side panel then shows its own session_key, distinct from the source's.\n\nEligibility comes from two fields on the session entry: native_fork (the runtime's capability bit on RuntimeDefinition — codex ✓ claude-code ✓ trae ✗) and forkable (native_fork ∧ key present ∧ direct chat ∧ not archived). Sidebar: the ⑂ is a hover affordance, so it has no disabled state — it renders only for a tab with exactly one non-shell pane whose chat is forkable; grouped tabs never show it (which chat? — fork those from the header). Header: the ⑂ acts on the focused pane; hidden for shell/empty panes; disabled with a tooltip when native_fork is false (\"Forking needs claude-code or codex\") or forkable is false (\"No session key captured yet\"); disabled without a tooltip while the fork is in flight.\n\nNot in v1: side-panel button, split-pane destination, ⋯ menu rows, shortcut, MCP tool. Spec: docs/features/60-fork-chat-to-pane-or-tab.md · plan: docs/impls/fork-chat.md",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JJSoc",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 78,
