          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JY46k",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "Two changes to a split tab. Focus is brightness, not a frame: the accent border goes, the divider is the only chrome, every unfocused pane's grid fades to 70 % with the terminal background (Ghostty's default), the identity line keeps its own focus colors. Splitting is a menu: the header icon opens Split Right / Left / Up / Down on the focused pane (Zed's shape), the same four end every ⋯, the preset picker and its three-pane ceiling are gone.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
