        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HMRnR",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 971,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "THE RULE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Q91QY",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 993,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "FOCUS IS BRIGHTNESS, NOT A FRAME — the focused pane has no border, and the transparent placeholder border on the others goes with it. Every unfocused pane in a split has its body drawn at 70 % opacity: the grid, its selection and cursor, and whatever sits over the grid (the ended card, the empty stub) dim together. Ghostty dims the whole split the same way (unfocused-split-opacity 0.7).\n\nTHE DIVIDER IS THE ONLY CHROME — the 1 px line inside the 5 px resize gutter, unchanged. THE IDENTITY LINE DOES NOT DIM — it carries focus in its own colors, and its status dot must stay readable while a working agent sits in a faded pane.\n\nONE SPLIT ICON PER PANE, TWO DIRECTIONS — Split Right ⌘D · Split Down ⇧⌘D. The icon lives with the pane it splits: the header's on a single-pane tab, the identity line's once split (beside ⋯, always visible; the header icon goes). Each item turns that pane's leaf into a 50 / 50 split with a new empty pane on that side; the new pane takes focus and shows the empty stub. The picker with its six presets and three-pane ceiling is gone; three columns is two Split Right clicks. The only limit is a size floor: 240 × 160 px per resulting pane at 1× zoom, scaled with app zoom.\n\nUNCHANGED — ⋯ (Stop · Rename… · Archive chat), single-pane tabs otherwise, the mission workspace, terminal drawers, secondary windows, the empty stub and the ended cards, click-to-focus, keyboard focus moves, × / ⌘W collapse, resize drag. Both theme modes. No settings.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Etbw2",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 971,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "WHAT CHANGES IN CODE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "YT0Wy",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 993,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "BORDER — panes.rs:2345 `.when(grouped, border_1().border_color(accent | transparent))` is removed.\n\nFADE — the pane body container in render_pane (the element that stacks the terminal and its overlay, panes.rs:1855 onward) gets `.opacity(UNFOCUSED_PANE_OPACITY)` when grouped && !focused, one constant at 0.7; the identity line sits outside it. GPUI element opacity reaches every quad and glyph painted underneath, the terminal element included, so the grid, cursor, ended card and empty stub dim together and nothing is overlaid; hitboxes, hover, cursor style and scrolling are untouched. Own PR.\n\nLAYOUT TREE — PaneLayout::split(pane_id, orientation) → new pane id. Persist the tree (splits: orientation, sizes, id; leaves: session id) instead of preset + slots + sizes; a legacy reader rebuilds the six preset trees from old rows, rewritten on next save. Leaf ids p<n> (next unused per tab), split ids s<n>. apply_preset, next_split_preset, derive_preset, canonicalize_split_ids, render_layout_picker (panes.rs:1338), pick_preset (chat.rs:1660) and split_pane (chat.rs:1717) go with the picker.\n\nICON + MENU — the header icon (panes.rs:400) renders only for single-pane tabs and opens a two-item UiMenu in the ⋯ popover's shape; the identity line gains the same icon beside ⋯ when grouped, opening the same menu for its pane; ⌘D / ⇧⌘D call the split on the focused pane; the size gate reads the pane's last laid-out bounds. Second PR with the tree.\n\nTESTS — split right and down on a root and a nested leaf; serialize round-trip; the six legacy presets decode to the trees they built; the size gate; TerminalStyle defaults to not dimmed; the fade constant pinned.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "Y2nbs",
          "x": 1107,
          "y": 164,
          "name": "fade_b_right",
          "fill": "#15161B4D",
          "width": 350,
          "height": 226
        },
