        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yQkub",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 911,
          "name": "cap_d_note",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1432,
          "content": "Left: a single-pane tab — the header keeps today's split icon and it opens the two-item menu. Right: once split, each identity line carries the same icon beside ⋯ (always visible, like ⋯ and ×) and the header icon goes; the menu splits that pane. Each item turns the pane into a 50 / 50 split with a new empty pane on that side, which takes focus. ⌘D / ⇧⌘D act on the focused pane. An item disables with the tooltip “Too small to split” when a resulting pane would be under 240 × 160 px at 1× zoom. No preset list, no pane count, no left or up, nothing new in ⋯.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "ITbDO",
      "x": 6860,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Drag to reorder panes (568) · v1",
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 873,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "l27EEI",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Drag to reorder panes (568) · v1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HMfwp",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "Ghostty 1.3's grab handle, on Runner's identity line. A faint grip sits in the line's free space on every pane of a split; hover brightens it and shows the hand; drag it and a pill with the pane's name follows the pointer. Every other pane takes four drops by nearest edge — left, right, up, down — each a move of the dragged pane to that side at 50 / 50, with the destination half lit as the preview. No center drop, no swap. Leaves move with their ids, so nothing remounts.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
