        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "eBAuc",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 360,
          "name": "cap_c_note",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "New terminal with a terminal tab active is the same as Split Right: it goes through the same gate and the same floor instead of prepare_new_pane. The empty-pane stub is never shown on a terminal tab. The drawer icon stays hidden on terminal tabs, as today.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Q4Ep97",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 570,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "THE RULE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Nh8Uf",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 592,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "A SPLIT IS A SPLIT — a terminal tab shows the same split icon (header when single, identity line when grouped), the same Split Right ⌘D / Split Down ⇧⌘D, the same 50 / 50 tree and the same 240 × 160 floor as a chat tab.\n\nTHE NEW PANE IS NEVER EMPTY — a shell spawns in it at once and takes focus, in the working directory the split-from pane's shell was spawned with (Ghostty: a split means another shell here, now). Live cwd through OSC 7 is a follow-up issue.\n\nNO MIXING, BY TAB KIND — a terminal tab's split makes a terminal, a chat tab's split makes the chat stub, the drawer stays the terminal home beside a chat.\n\nNEW TERMINAL ON A TERMINAL TAB = SPLIT RIGHT — same gate, same floor.\n\nUNCHANGED — grip and drag (568), ×, ⋯ (Stop · Rename…), rename, the drawer, chat tabs, the mission workspace.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ugjLo",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 570,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "WHAT CHANGES IN CODE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lbLOV",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 592,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "GATE — split_decision (panes.rs) drops the terminal-only → NotSplittable arm; the header split icon renders on a terminal-only single-pane tab (panes.rs:398); the drawer icon still does not.\n\nSPLIT — chat.rs split_pane: after layout.split, when the tab is terminal-only, spawn a shell into the new pane with spawn_terminal_in_pane (start_chat.rs) using the split-from session's cwd, then the same persist → reload → attach → focus; otherwise the empty stub as today.\n\nNEW TERMINAL — new_terminal_target Tab on a terminal-only tab calls split_pane(focused, Row) instead of prepare_new_pane, so the floor applies.\n\nTESTS — split_decision on a terminal-only tab: allowed, blocked by size; new terminal on a full terminal tab meets the floor. DOCS — arch.md pane paragraph, the 64 smoke test §1.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "esVJZ",
      "x": 10140,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Session status (347) · v1 · vocabulary",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 680,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PnHav",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Hook-based session status (347) · v1 · vocabulary",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "FPVY8",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "Today a session is one 5px dot: amber Busy, green Idle, grey Stopped, red Crashed — guessed from a title spinner and byte traffic. Lifecycle hooks let the agent say what it is doing, so status becomes a 12px glyph with an 11px label. Working, Needs you and Idle are the everyday states; lifecycle and observability supply the rest. Muted = normal, amber = you, red = error, accent = unread — and shape plus label separates every state without relying on colour.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "BbSCv",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 100,
          "name": "EVERYDAY — WHAT THE AGENT IS DOING",
          "width": 468,
