          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "The row layout and the runtime icon stay exactly as they are; only the trailing 12px attention slot gains the new states. One slot shows one thing, in priority order — unresolved error, needs you, working, unread completion, status unavailable, nothing — and the tooltip lists everything the dominant glyph is covering, so the row never silently erases a second condition. Status unavailable ranks last because it is missing knowledge, not a call for attention; it is still drawn, because an empty slot reads as quiet and ready. A ready tab you are already looking at stays quiet.",
