        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "y6Xmj",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 700,
          "name": "note_b",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "The mission row aggregates its runners and must never call a whole mission Idle because one runner is — mission outcomes keep coming from mission events, and a queued inbox message is not the same thing as an agent asking you to approve or answer. Clicking the row's indicator opens the affected runner. The pending-asks and inbox surfaces stay as they are: a Runner ask that already supplies an interaction identity is counted once, not twice.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "wLIlB",
      "x": 10140,
      "y": 3513,
      "name": "Light — Session status vocabulary (347)",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "light"
      },
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 680,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hIegj",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Hook-based session status (347) · v1 · vocabulary",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "A6ljzt",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "Today a session is one 5px dot: amber Busy, green Idle, grey Stopped, red Crashed — guessed from a title spinner and byte traffic. Lifecycle hooks let the agent say what it is doing, so status becomes a 12px glyph with an 11px label. Working, Needs you and Idle are the everyday states; lifecycle and observability supply the rest. Muted = normal, amber = you, red = error, accent = unread — and shape plus label separates every state without relying on colour.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "xI7qY",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 100,
          "name": "EVERYDAY — WHAT THE AGENT IS DOING",
          "width": 468,
          "fill": "$panel",
          "cornerRadius": 9,
          "stroke": "$border",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 9,
          "padding": 14,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z6RnxC",
              "name": "cap",
              "fill": "$text-low",
              "content": "EVERYDAY — WHAT THE AGENT IS DOING",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "EXgM9",
              "name": "note",
              "fill": "$text-mid",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The three states a user reads all day. Tool detail and the reason for a wait live in secondary text, never in a new colour.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
