                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "JuxCD",
                      "name": "n",
                      "fill": "$text-mid",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "$text-1 is #DCDCE0 in Carbon and #1C1D22 in Runner Light, so the Codex knot inverts with the theme the way cmux ships two appearance variants of the same asset — one tint, two grounds, no second file.\n\n#D97757 is fixed. It is the only colour in the rail that is not a theme token, which is the point: it says Claude, not selected.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PinWy",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1081,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "RULES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GtCM6",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1103,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "The mark comes from the runtime stored on the session, and from nothing else. Not the window title, not the process table, not the model. A chat started from a runner template resolves through the same field, so a template and a hand-started chat of the same runtime look identical.\n\nIdentity is the hue; life is the opacity. The rail today says “something is running in here” by painting the icon in the accent and dropping it to muted when nothing is — the same signal the mission flag and the project folder use. A brand tint that ignored liveness would spend that reading, so the mark keeps one hue in every state and renders dimmed, beside the label that already goes faint, when no member session is running. 0.45 against the row's own 1.0, the app's existing dimming idiom.\n\nSelection and focus stay where they are. A selected row is still its fill, border and semibold label; a focused pane is still its header text and body opacity. The mark answers neither, so no row ever has two things changing colour at once.\n\nStatus is still #347's. Working, Needs you and Ready keep their own glyph and their own colours at the other end of the row, and the mark never takes them on, never turns into an unread marker, and never replaces an attention badge.\n\nRenaming a chat, changing its model, archiving and restoring it, dragging its pane, or resuming it after a relaunch never changes the mark. Stopping it only dims it.\n\nOne mark per provider, or none at all. A runtime we have no mark for keeps the speech bubble, and no provider's logo is ever borrowed as another's fallback — a wrong logo is worse than a generic one.\n\nA tab is not a pane. A split tab keeps columns-2 / columns-3: the tab stands for a group, and a group holding two providers has no single mark. A single-pane tab shows its one pane's mark, in the rail and in the workspace header alike.\n\nShell keeps the terminal glyph, empty panes keep square-dashed, and generic actions and categories — New chat, Chats, Settings → Agents — keep their own symbols. This feature answers who you are talking to, not what a control does.\n\nClaude is #D97757 and Trae is #32F08C in both themes, the only colours in the rail that are not theme tokens. Codex takes $text-1, so it inverts with the ground instead of shipping a second asset.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XgARC",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1081,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "IMPLEMENTATION",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TqDDx",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1103,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "GPUI rasterises an SVG as a mask and paints it in one colour: window.paint_svg(bounds, path, None, transform, color) takes a single tint from style.text.color, so a fill baked into the file is discarded. All three marks are single-path, so nothing is lost — but Claude's orange and Trae's green have to be written at the call site, not carried by the asset.\n\nThe marks join the lucide glyphs as byte constants in crates/runner-app/src/assets.rs and one row each in ASSETS. Sources to record beside them: the Claude starburst and the OpenAI knot from Orca (c1e15c4), the Trae screen from lobe-icons' static-svg set. Nothing is fetched at runtime; the app must draw all three offline on macOS and Windows.\n\nOne shared mapping in runner-app turns a runtime key into an asset path and a tint, and every identity call site goes through it: sidebar/menus.rs::sidebar_tab_icon, sidebar/rows_render.rs with its icon, inline-rename and drag presentation, and panes.rs::pane_identity_icon. workspace_header_icon takes a grouped/focused-shell bool pair today and needs the focused pane's runtime instead.\n\nsidebar_icon(path, live) is where liveness lives today — it paints accent when live and muted when not, and rows_render.rs passes `live`, not `active`, at all three call sites. For a provider mark the tint stops varying and the element takes opacity instead; the shell, layout, mission-flag and project-folder glyphs keep the accent/muted pair exactly as they are.\n\nsurfaces/command_palette.rs and surfaces/settings/archived.rs already hold the runtime on their items and then pick an icon from the generic item kind; the runtime has to reach the presentation item rather than being dropped there. Archived rows are stopped by definition, so they render dimmed.\n\nThe icon assertions that exist today — pane_identity_icon in panes.rs, sidebar_tab_icon in sidebar/tests.rs — expect message-square for claude-code and codex and become the new paths; assets.rs gets a registration test beside the ones already there.\n\nNo database migration, no new preference, no terminal-title parsing, no process detection, and no change to session lifecycle or status detection.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "IHxWT",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1556,
          "name": "prior_art",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "PRIOR ART — Orca maps Claude to its starburst and Codex to the OpenAI knot in one shared AgentIcon, keeps #D97757 in the file and lets everything else inherit currentColor, and gives an unknown identity a neutral fallback. cmux bundles branded assets per agent and ships explicit light and dark variants of the Codex image, falling back to a system symbol when an asset is missing. Runner takes the mapping from the first and the offline-assets-with-a-tint discipline from the second, and needs neither an asset catalogue nor a second file per theme because the mask is tinted at paint time.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "O9Qgf",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 822,
          "name": "cap_g",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "G · LIVENESS — TODAY THE RAIL SAYS “SOMETHING IS RUNNING IN HERE” WITH THE ICON'S COLOUR; A FIXED BRAND TINT WOULD SPEND THAT, SO THE HUE STAYS AND THE OPACITY CARRIES IT",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
