                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "N26F1",
                      "name": "n",
                      "fill": "$text-mid",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "#8534F3 stays fixed on both grounds, like Claude's orange and Trae's green; on Runner Light it sits near 4.5:1, better than the Trae green. Only the Codex knot flips with $text-1, so the rail keeps four distinct hues in both themes.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "c8Vix",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1000,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "RULES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KXp5P",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1022,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "The mark is identity, never state (#593). Copilot's mark holds one hue in every row — selected or not, Working, Needs you or Idle — and dims to 0.45 when no member session is running. Status stays with the #347 glyph and the unread dot.\n\nA wrong logo is worse than a generic one. Until the runtime enum knows `copilot`, a Copilot session is an unknown runtime and draws the speech bubble; the mark appears only once the session's stored runtime is `copilot`.\n\nThe Agents row, the runtime pickers, the permission dropdown and the Skills pane are the shipped components with new words. Nothing on this frame is a new control.\n\nWindows draws the same mark from the same bundled bytes. There is no per-theme second file; the tint is applied at paint time.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "h7CJl",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1000,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "IMPLEMENTATION",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "IZ9cU",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1022,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "assets.rs: `COPILOT` from lobe-icons `githubcopilot.svg` at the pinned commit. The goggles already fill their 24-box, so keep `viewBox 0 0 24 24` unless it looks heavy beside the others at 12 px, whose files use `-2 -2 28 28` for optical padding. One `ASSETS` row, `copilot.svg`; the MIT block already carries the LobeHub line.\n\nchat_icon.rs: `Some(Runtime::Copilot) => (\"copilot.svg\", gpui::rgb(0x8534f3).into())` — GitHub's Copilot Purple, fixed in both themes. Every identity surface already routes through `ChatIcon::for_runtime`, so no other call site changes.\n\nTests: `pane_identity_icon`, `sidebar_tab_icon`, `command_palette.rs`, `settings/archived.rs`, the `assets.rs` registration test and the `chat_icon.rs` tint table each gain a `copilot` row.\n\nThe D copy goes into `runners/logic.rs::permission_mode_description` verbatim. The Agents row needs nothing beyond the catalog entry.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Xk8NM",
      "x": 23020,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Rail glyphs (606) · v1",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 1020,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bXNNP",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Rail glyphs (606) · v1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nDqwS",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "The rail runs two rules at once: folders, the shell glyph and the mission flag say “live” with the accent green, while provider marks say identity with a fixed hue and “live” with opacity. This frame makes it one rule — hue is identity and only provider marks have one; everything else is neutral and dims when nothing runs; the accent stays at the tail for state — and gives the folder a closed and an open state next to the chevron that already flips. Decided 2026-09-16: the lucide outline pair.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XlGU5",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 100,
          "name": "cap_a",
