                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "cKiIP",
                  "name": "n",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "State lives at the tail and in the chrome, never at the head of a row. The Working spinner stays muted per #347 (amber is for human attention), so in the rail the accent is exactly three things: the ready dot, the unread pill, and the drag-and-drop indicator. A folder, a shell glyph or a flag never turns green again.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GX4po",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 560,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "RULES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "POl8N",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 582,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "Hue is identity, and only provider marks have one (#593). Every other head-of-row glyph — folder, shell, layout, flag — is $text-1 in both themes.\n\nLiveness is opacity, for every glyph. Full strength when a member session is running, 0.45 when none is, beside the label that already drops to faint. An inactive row dims as one unit.\n\nThe accent is state, and state sits at the tail or in the chrome: ready dot, unread pill, drop indicator. The mission flag stops duplicating the spinner next to it, and the Trae mark stops colliding with a green folder above it.\n\nThe folder has two states, chosen by the project's expansion, next to the chevron that already flips. Closed when collapsed, open when expanded. The <> badge goes; every project is a code project.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "MFCu9",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 800,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "IMPLEMENTATION",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "fpI3E",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 822,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "sidebar_icon(icon, live) in surfaces/sidebar: for a generic icon return theme::text() with opacity 1.0 / 0.45 instead of the accent/muted pair; provider marks keep their branch. Callers in rows_render.rs pass the same `live` they pass today: the project header (folder), the mission row (flag), and sidebar_tab_icon for shell and layout tabs.\n\nassets.rs: the closed folder joins the bundled folder-open.svg (both lucide, MIT); folder-code.svg is removed once nothing references it. The project header picks folder.svg or folder-open.svg from `collapsed`, where it already picks the chevron.\n\nTests: the colour table in chat_icon.rs, sidebar_tab_icon, and a project-header test for the asset by expansion state. No backend change, no migration.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Lgki9",
      "x": 24600,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Brand mark exploration · v1",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 720,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "bAMC2",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Brand mark exploration · v1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CuPKs",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "The mark today is three thin chevrons with two ghosts at 40 %: a terminal prompt, which is the right idea — agent-agnostic and name-agnostic, so it survives the rebrand either way — drawn so that it goes wispy on the dock and reads as “>” plus noise at 16 px. Three directions keep the prompt and fix the drawing: equal weight, strokes that hold at 16 px, and a composition that says something. Formation says crew-with-a-lead; column says a roster of sessions; trail says motion. Each is shown as the dock tile, the sidebar lockup, 16 px, the light theme, and one-colour.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Iv81Z",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 100,
          "name": "directions",
          "width": 1452,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 18,
