        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DM5aR",
          "x": 790,
          "y": 422,
          "name": "note_c",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 686,
          "content": "A single-pane row is the pane, so its tooltip is the pane's and ends with the elapsed time. Rollups keep counting: 1 approval needed · 1 working, with no clock, because a count of waits is the signal and the oldest one is what a click opens. The row's amber glyph, the project and section rollups and the mission row are all unchanged. The mission tab strip keeps the glyph only.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "zbeMW",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 566,
          "name": "footer",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "RULES — Elapsed is now minus the interaction's since, per interaction; with several waits open the pane reports its oldest, which is also the one a rollup click opens. Seconds under a minute, whole minutes under an hour, then hours and minutes. The card redraws on the minute, the tooltip every second while shown. Time never changes colour, precedence, ordering or delivery. No timer on Working, Idle or errors: silence never changes a state, and a long turn is not a wait.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "bqwlq",
      "x": 31080,
      "y": 1693,
      "name": "Spec — Status details (624) · v1 · failure attention",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "height": 610,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AF2MP",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Status details (624) · v1 · failure attention",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "m8Z7Mi",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "Response failed shipped in 347 as a pane-header label with no sidebar presence, so a failed turn in a pane out of view was invisible. It now raises attention the way an exited process does: the red alert glyph in the row's slot, its own count in every rollup, and the same acknowledgement rule. The pane's own label stays until the next turn.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kiFSZ",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 96,
