        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WlXvK",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 470,
          "name": "note_b",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "The runner card is the 347 card: red glyph, red label, no change. The mission row counts the failure among its runners and shows the alert glyph when it is the dominant condition; clicking the indicator opens the failed runner. The mission tab strip shows the same glyph on the runner's tab, as it did in 347.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "F4IKbL",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 536,
          "name": "footer",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "RULES — Response failed ranks with error: above needs-you, working, unread and unavailable, in the row and in every rollup. Tooltips list it as its own count next to error, so a failed turn and an exited process are never merged. Attention is acknowledged by viewing the pane, like error; a rollup click opens the oldest unresolved error or failure first. Source today: Claude Code's StopFailure. Copilot's ErrorOccurred joins once a live fatal fixture lands; Codex publishes no fatal-failure hook. Baseline sessions never claim a failure.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Jlvgd",
      "x": 26220,
      "y": 1600,
      "name": "statusDetailsLbl",
      "fill": "$text-2",
      "content": "STATUS DETAILS (624) — the deferred 347 details: Working · Using tools / Compacting context, the interrupted outcome, wait timers, and sidebar attention for a failed response. Details live in the header label, the tab bar and the card (Jason, 2026-09-17: nobody hovers); the tooltip repeats them. The nonblocking ask is cut.",
      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontWeight": "500"
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "zVywQ",
      "x": 23020,
      "y": 2793,
      "name": "Spec — Session liveness in the rail · v3",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1500,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "o7cF0V",
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — Session liveness in the rail · v3",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ywbtd",
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Keep #606's dim, change one thing: a stopped provider mark loses its hue. Today a stopped Claude mark is still orange at 0.45, and colour is the first thing the eye reads, so a stopped chat still looks on. Drawn grey, like a stopped Codex mark, folder or flag, the rail's colour means running. No new element, no idle decoration; idle rows look exactly as they do today.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
