        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "qjnDb",
          "name": "notes",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 32,
          "padding": [
            14,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "gnFXu",
              "name": "rules",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 8,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "S0rJ8a",
                  "name": "cap",
                  "fill": "$text-low",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "RULE",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hVwLQ",
                  "name": "body",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A provider mark keeps its hue only while its session is running. Stopped, it draws in the same neutral as every other stopped glyph — $text-1 at 0.45 — so colour in the rail means running, and the shape still says which agent it is. The label dim, the tail states and the running rows are unchanged.\n\nCodex is already monochrome, so a Codex row gains nothing: its running and stopped rows still differ by brightness alone. That is the one case this does not fix.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HM7DR",
                  "name": "cap",
                  "fill": "$text-low",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "IMPLEMENTATION",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "C88Ls",
                  "name": "body",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "chat_icon.rs: ChatIcon::color returns the neutral stopped colour when !live instead of the tint at 0.45. It is the one colour function for provider marks, so the sidebar, pane headers and the command palette follow together. The colour table test in chat_icon.rs flips its not-live assertion. No backend change.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "K3YTMR",
              "name": "why",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 8,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "mAdW9",
                  "name": "cap",
                  "fill": "$text-low",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "NOT PURSUED (2026-09-17)",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "qQuDY",
                  "name": "body",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Idle ring, idle dot, idle dot with grey marks: idle should not carry a decoration. Stopped rows showing when they stopped: stopped_at is only real for an explicit stop or exit — after a force quit, crash or reboot it is the next launch time, and after a normal quit it is the quit. A rail line beside running rows, and folding stopped chats under their project.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "S5BDBL",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -400,
      "name": "ARCHIVE-MARKER chat-feature-specs",
      "width": 900,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "Archive — chat feature specs, moved out of design/runner.pen on 2026-09-19.\n\nShipped features only. Frame ids are unchanged, so the archived feature docs and briefs that name a frame id still resolve here. Components are a snapshot of runner.pen from that day."
    }
  ],
